{
  "$comment": [
    "Installed to <theme-repo>/.claude/settings.json at STEP 0 of /build-page — before any pipeline",
    "command runs. v3 installed it at step 1 (bootstrap), which meant you needed permission to run",
    "the bootstrap that installed the permissions. Chicken-and-egg; fixed here.",
    "",
    "v4.1 (2026-09): defaultMode 'auto' (the v4 default) was NOT honoured by the Claude desktop app —",
    "every compound Bash call prompted and a human sat clicking for a run that was supposed to be",
    "unattended. What worked: defaultMode 'bypassPermissions' + 'Bash(*)' in allow + the deny list",
    "below, which is evaluated first and still blocks the irreversible operations. The allowlist is",
    "kept so a client that DOES honour allow/deny semantics stays scoped.",
    "Commit this file: a run that prompts on one machine and not another is not reproducible.",
    "",
    "FIGMA SERVER NAMES: v3 allowlisted 'mcp__figma__*', which matches NO server that exists —",
    "MCP permission rules match the normalized server name exactly. Rules below cover the servers",
    "commonly present: 'Figma' (desktop app), 'figma-console' (REST/Desktop Bridge),",
    "'plugin_figma_figma' (official plugin). A claude.ai connector is NOT listed in ~/.claude.json;",
    "add its 'mcp__<connector-id>__<tool>' rules here and set F2S_FIGMA_SERVERS for permcheck.",
    "f2s_permcheck.sh checks these prefixes and tells you if none match."
  ],
  "permissions": {
